  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">El Amatillo-Honduras: Creating Resilience and Employment for Communities in Remote Environments (CRECER)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to generate economic opportunities and promote productive and decent work mainly for informal and unemployed workers and people involved in menial economic activities located at the border area of El Amatillo. 

To achieve its objective, the project will identify business activities and occupations for the selected beneficiary group(s), develop a comprehensive skills development training program, prepare the beneficiaries to successfully run their joint operated business and enhance the image and visibility of the border area to attract new businesses.

By doing so, the project expects to reduce the level of dependency of border communities on income derived from informal activities at the border and their propensity to migrate.</narrative>
  </description>
